title: Psalms 38–40: Godly Sorrow, the Measure of My Days, and a New Song
description: Psalms 38-40 in the King James Bible: rebuke me not in thy wrath, Cain's sorrow and David's godly sorrow, the bridle on the tongue and the measure of my days, what wait I for, the horrible pit and the new song, and sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire, from the Psalms series studies.
output: lessons/bible/psalms-38-40.html
context: yes

